cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Paul Graham, Distilled — Five Claude Code Skills + Six Principles"
message: "If you reference this distillation in your own work, please cite both this repository and Paul Graham's original essays."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "WinterDDo"
    given-names: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/WinterDDo/paul-graham-skills"
abstract: >-
  A distillation of Paul Graham's essays into two parallel outputs: five
  Claude Code execution skills (loadable behavioral disciplines for AI
  agents) and six principles for human cognition (essay-form synthesis).
  The skills and principles are derived from approximately 37 of PG's
  essays read with two distinct filters: 'what describes a Claude
  execution behavior?' (skills) and 'what describes a thinking
  discipline a human should internalize?' (principles).
keywords:
  - claude-code
  - claude-skills
  - paul-graham
  - prompt-engineering
  - llm-tools
  - ai-agents
  - anthropic
license: MIT
references:
  - type: collection
    title: "Paul Graham's Essays"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Graham"
        given-names: "Paul"
    url: "https://paulgraham.com/articles.html"
